<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upper Rhenish Circle</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1500–1806</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Upper Rhenish Circle was one of the Imperial Circles of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, created in 1500 to organise defence, taxation and the keeping of the peace. It grouped many small territories along the middle and upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> and in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, including Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a>, Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a>, the Nassau and Hanau counties and the bishoprics of Worms, Speyer and Strasbourg. It ended with the Empire in 1806.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/upper-rhenish-circle.jpg" alt="Upper Rhenish Circle" width="320" height="313" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sir Iain · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Locator_Upper-Rhenisch_Circle.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
